          "transcript": "[Talk 1: Pedal Power Charity]<br/><span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 21</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">I decided to join a voluntary organization and was sent to Ecuador...</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 22</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">Then I realized having a bike meant he could get where he wanted to go without much trouble...</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 23</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">But in order to continue operating we need to have a constant supply of bikes...</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 24</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">The local economy has developed so much, you wouldn't recognise it...</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 25</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">In August 2000, we simply ran out of money. We had containers of bikes ready to send but no money to pay the bills.</span><br/><br/>[Talk 2: Environmental Noise]<br/><span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 26</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">The only noise after dark is from the highway, and the traffic is somewhat reduced between 7:30 pm and 5:30 am.</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 27</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">So, the people most affected by the noise will be, I expect, housewives...</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 28</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">The weekends are still a problem of course, but the traffic is certainly reduced on Saturdays to a large extent and even more so on Sundays...</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 29</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">The modifications I am about to outline will add about $25,000 to the price...</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 30</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">Of course, those nearest the highway will be the worst hit, with heavy traffic noise as well as the noise from the light planes overhead.</span><br/><br/>[Talk 3: Household waste recycled]<br/><span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 31</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">my group has been doing a project on how household waste is recycled in Britain...</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 32</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">The agreed targets for the UK mean that by 2008 we must reduce our carbon dioxide emissions by 12.5 percent...</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 33</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">The production of recycled glass and paper uses much less energy...</span> <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 34</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">One problem here is taking out everything that shouldn't have been placed in the recycling containers.</span> People put all sorts of things into bottle banks... Two million tons of glass is thrown away each year... <span class=\"vstep-q-badge\">Câu 35</span><span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">But only 500,000 tons of that is collected and recycled.</span>",
