              "transcriptSnippet": "[Talk 3: Household waste recycled]<br/>my group has been doing a project on how household waste is recycled in Britain... The agreed targets for the UK mean that by 2008 we must reduce our carbon dioxide emissions by 12.5 percent... The production of recycled glass and paper uses much less energy... One problem here is taking out everything that shouldn't have been placed in the recycling containers. People put all sorts of things into bottle banks... Two million tons of glass is thrown away each year... <span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">But only 500,000 tons of that is collected and recycled.</span>",
