              "transcriptSnippet": "Conversation 1 (Questions 9-12)<br/>Speaker 1: Good morning, may I help you?<br/>Speaker 2: Yes, I'm Mark Winston and I...<br/>Speaker 1: Oh, excuse me, Mr. Winston. World Language Academy, this is Kathy Green, may I help you? No, this is a private language school, not a travel agency. No problem at all. Goodbye. I'm sorry, Mr. Winston. Now, may I help you?<br/>Speaker 2: Yes, I hope you can. <span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">I'd like to sign up now for a Japanese class next week.</span><br/>Speaker 1: Classes start next week and we have lots of Japanese classes to choose from. Have you studied Japanese before?<br/>Speaker 2: No, I haven't. I'm a beginner. I'm planning to visit Japan next summer, so I want to learn a bit of the language.<br/>Speaker 1: That's great. Japan is a wonderful place to visit. I spent a month in Tokyo last year actually, and I even climbed Mount Fujiyama.<br/>Speaker 2: Really? That's too much activity for me. I'm just planning to visit Tokyo. I think I'll find plenty to do there.<br/>Speaker 1: You certainly will. All right then, let me tell you a bit about our classes. They're all taught by native speakers, and they're all specialists in their field. You can choose a Japanese for Tourists class, Japanese for Business Travelers, or Japanese for University Students. You're not studying at a university, are you?<br/>Speaker 2: No, I graduated a few years ago.<br/>Speaker 1: Well then the Tourist class is probably best for you.<br/>Speaker 2: Yes, I think you're right. I just want to learn enough to order food in restaurants and go shopping and things like that. When does the Japanese for Tourists class begin?<br/>Speaker 1: Let's see... We have a class for beginners that starts next week. I think there are still a few spaces left. You're in luck. We have 15 students enrolled, and there's room for three more.",
