              "transcriptSnippet": "Conversation 2 (Questions 13-16)<br/>Speaker 1: Hello, have you come to enroll for your course or pay your fees?<br/>Speaker 2: Um, both actually.<br/>Speaker 1: Okay, that's fine. You can enroll here with me and then go to the next desk for fee payment. So, first of all, can I have your name?<br/>Speaker 2: <span class=\"text-red-600 font-bold bg-yellow-100 px-1 rounded mx-1 answer-hl\">Yes, it's Peter Taylor.</span> That's Taylor with a Y.<br/>Speaker 1: So, it's T-A-Y-L-O-R.<br/>Speaker 2: That's right. Do you need my middle name?<br/>Speaker 1: No, just your first and last names, thanks. And what course are you doing?<br/>Speaker 2: I'm taking a BSC in Economics.<br/>Speaker 1: Okay, that's in the Faculty of Mathematics.<br/>Speaker 2: Oh, I thought it was in the Faculty of Business and Management.<br/>Speaker 1: It was last year, but the course has moved to the Mathematics Faculty this year.<br/>Speaker 2: Oh, thanks for letting me know.<br/>Speaker 1: No problem. Now, where are you going to be living? On campus or in private accommodation?<br/>Speaker 2: University accommodation. I'm in room 112, Ashley Residence.<br/>Speaker 1: Did you say Ashley Residence? The one in Duke Street? It's just that there's another residence called Ashkey Residence, so it's confusing sometimes. I don't want to make a mistake on the computer records, otherwise you won't receive any university mail.<br/>Speaker 2: It's definitely Ashley. A-S-H-L-E-Y.<br/>Speaker 1: Great. And what about your home address? On our records, it says 56 Grove Street, Manchester, M1 9JA. Is that correct?<br/>Speaker 2: Actually, there's a small mistake. It's M4, not M1. The rest is correct, 9JA.<br/>Speaker 1: Okay, I think that's all. You're enrolled on your course, so you can go and pay your fees now.<br/>Speaker 2: Thanks, bye.",
